# Cursor Rules Standards

## Location

- Cursor rules must be stored in `.cursor/rules/` directory
- Do not use `.cursorrules` file in root (legacy format)

## File Format

- Use `.mdc` (Markdown Domain Configuration) file extension
- Include frontmatter with `description` and `globs` fields
- Frontmatter format:
  ```yaml
  ---
  description: Brief summary of rule purpose
  globs: file patterns (e.g., **/*, *.py, CHANGELOG.md)
  ---
  ```

## Organization

- Create focused, single-purpose rule files
- Name files descriptively (e.g., `contributing.mdc`, `changelog.mdc`)
- Reference main documentation files rather than duplicating content
- Keep rules concise and actionable
